From d3e331951b60a9f36baee7ee175f1eed2e60f319 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:42:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] dotnet: serve Pages from gh-pages holding only the
 manifest files

The .NET shapes (console, desktop, maui) served Pages from main's root so
the dashboard could fetch src-manifest.json. A Pages site is public even
when the repo is private, so that put every file on main one URL away from
anyone: the source, docs, TODO.md, CLAUDE.md.

- manifest-dotnet.yml: after committing the outputs to main as before,
  publish src-manifest.json, src-symbols.json, src-tours.json and
  src-book.json (those that exist) plus .nojekyll to gh-pages as a single
  rebuilt commit. Nothing is pushed when the branch's tree already matches.
- claude-book.yml: a book run on a .NET shape publishes the same files to
  gh-pages after its commit, since that commit carries [skip ci].
- onboard.sh: .NET shapes create gh-pages when it is missing, seeded with
  the outputs the target already has, then point Pages at gh-pages/root
  (POST to create the site, PUT to move an existing one). A repo onboarded
  earlier is moved by its next refresh. SQL and served-from-source are
  unchanged.
- README.md, SHAPES.md: Pages source per shape.

The dashboard's URLs do not change.
